invariant: INV-26
file: gcm.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: a QUIC host object runs GHASH on the carry-less multiply and
  counter mode's whole blocks on the AES instructions for a schedule the
  table runs, so a session whose caller did not set
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES executes PMULL or PCLMULQDQ and the AES
  instructions on every Initial packet. Both paths compute the same bytes,
  so no vector notices. bin/aes_runtime_test seals and opens Initial
  packets without the bit: aes_encrypt_counter_blocks's assertion that its
  schedule runs on the instructions stops it at the first seal, and it
  also counts the calls into ghash_hw.c and requires none.

--- old
    return k->instructions == AES_ON_INSTRUCTIONS;
--- new
    return k->instructions != 0;
